<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pays d'Auge</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pays d’Auge</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pays d'Auge is a region of Normandy in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, lying between the valleys of the Touques and the Dives inland from the Channel coast, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisieux">Lisieux</a> as its main town. Its green hills and pastures are famous for dairy farming and cider orchards, producing Camembert, Livarot and Pont-l'Évêque cheeses and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calvados">Calvados</a> apple brandy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pays-d-auge.jpg" alt="Pays d'Auge" width="320" height="577" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillaume de L'Isle · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PaysdAuge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
